As I understand it, {mi du le ci nolraitru} is false, even if spoken by the 
three kings, because it asserts that each one of them is all three kings. But 
{mi du lei ci nolraitru} is correct when said by the kings, because {mi} 
refers to the set of speakers ({mi} is nonspecific as to individual/mass/set).

